   "body": "**mac/M1 (sub-agent mac/M1-i832-sonnet): draft #1086, head e60ba7b8. #1048 did not fix the landscape case.**\n\n- **Measured** in a hosted probe: a list as the window root, 932 × 430 and 874 × 402, landscape safe area 62 pt, compact density. Header text from the card edge: **92 pt** on 74d863c1 (69 before #1048); row text 59 pt; expected 7 and 7. With the notch on the right only, it was already 7/7.\n- **Cause 1:** `contentMargins(.horizontal, 10, .scrollContent)` replaces the system side inset, safe area included, so the card sat at x = 10, under the notch.\n- **Cause 2:** the header's card edge counted the inset twice: `originX + 10 + safeLeading`, while the list frame already starts at 62.\n- **Fix** (`DensityListMargins`, `ListDensity.swift`): the margins add the measured leading and trailing safe insets, and the card edge is the frame x plus the margin. `DensityHeaderMargin`, its cap and regular density are unchanged.\n- **Test:** `compactHeadersAlignInLandscape` (5 cases: both sizes; notch left, right, both) fails without the fix (6 issues) and passes with it. The whole `SwiftHFRTests` target passes (1,917).\n- **Still owed:** the device check in landscape, both notch sides, compact on and off (in the PR). The safe area was simulated with `additionalSafeAreaInsets`. Opus review running.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
